# UnkeyedActivityLogMessageRatchetGuard — the seeded inventory of `new LogMessage("…", level)`
# sites under src/ that carry NO `.WithKey(…)`, i.e. that persist rendered ENGLISH onto the node
# and can never be translated for the viewer who reads them (#3236).
#
# Format: <repo-relative path><TAB><count>.  The ratchet may only SHRINK: a new file, a raised
# count, or a raised TotalBudget is a failure.  Adding a line here is not a fix.
#
# 🚨 These eighteen are NOT a to-do list that nobody got to. #3281 migrated everything that was
# genuinely migratable; what is left is the two populations that cannot carry a key, and they are
# expected to stay:
#
#   GENERIC PLUMBING — an ILogger adapter, or a helper whose entire input is a `string message`
#   parameter. The site does not know a SENTENCE, so there is nothing to key. A caller that wants a
#   key builds the LogMessage itself and hands it to the batched overload
#   (NodeTypeCompilationActivity.AppendLogs / ActivityLogAppender.Append) — which is why migrating
#   one of these callers needs no signature change here.
#
#   VERBATIM UPSTREAM TEXT — ex.Message, a Roslyn diagnostic, a descendant hub's own refusal, a
#   composed multi-clause import summary. No catalog can carry these; a template reduced to a lone
#   {detail} placeholder would be a translation of nothing.
#
# The lines below say which is which. Where a site is genuinely migratable it is named as such and
# tracked on the follow-up issue, not blessed here.

# ILogger → activity adapter: the text arrives already formatted by an ILogger formatter.
src/MeshWeaver.Kernel.Hub/ActivityLogLogger.cs	1
# Same, plus the `string message` convenience on Activity itself.
src/MeshWeaver.Data/Activity.cs	2
# ActivityLog.Fail(string error) — the error is the caller's sentence, not this method's.
src/MeshWeaver.Data.Contract/ActivityLog.cs	1
# AppendLog(…, string message, …) and Update(…, string? error, …): `string message` plumbing. A
# caller with a sentence hands a keyed LogMessage to the BATCHED overload instead — which is what
# #3281 did to all three StaticRepoImporter callers, with no signature change here.
src/MeshWeaver.Compiler.Pipeline/NodeTypeCompilationActivity.cs	2
# AppendVerbatimWarning(log, message) — a Roslyn diagnostic, already formatted by the compiler with
# its own CS id and span. The Append{Info,Warning,Error} helpers beside it now REQUIRE a key (#3281),
# so this named exception is the only unkeyed way into the compile transcript.
src/MeshWeaver.Compiler.Pipeline/MeshNodeCompilationService.cs	1
# settle.Diagnosis — a post-condition verdict composed elsewhere.
src/MeshWeaver.Compiler.Pipeline/NodeTypeCompilationHelpers.cs	1
# All three are now the deliberate un-keyed spellings, after #3281 threaded LogMessage through the
# runner (RunActivity's LogMessage-title overload, ActivityContext.Log(LogMessage)) and migrated the
# eight GitHubActivityExtensions operations onto them: the `string title` forwarder, the
# `Log(string, level)` convenience, and the terminal line carrying the command's own ex.Message.
src/MeshWeaver.GitSync/ActivityRunner.cs	3
# f.Error (a descendant hub's own refusal), PostFail's `error` (which is also the response text) and
# the ex.Message arm of the terminal delete failure. All upstream text.
src/MeshWeaver.Mesh.Contract/MeshExtensions.cs	3
# Two composed multi-clause run summaries (each folds 6+ conditional notes carrying #604/#3101
# incident wording) and the stranded-instances report built by NodeTypeInstanceProbe. The
# content-sync ledger left this list in #3281 — LedgerNode now takes the LogMessage its two callers
# build, both keyed.
src/MeshWeaver.Graph/StaticRepoImporter.cs	3
# e.Message from a faulted submit.
src/MeshWeaver.Layout/Client/LayoutClientExtensions.cs	1
